TestShellFilesAndSessionState exercises real object messages for paths with spaces/metacharacters, read/write/append, directory creation, recursive search, literal text search and separate environment overrides. Assert failures signal and failed navigation preserves cwd.
TestShellChildProcess is a controlled subprocess reporting cwd, environment, stdin and a literal argument, with separate diagnostics and exit seven.
TestShellProcessStreamsInputAndEnvironment launches that subprocess through Shell, checks outputs and retained jobs, verifies inspect returns, rejects process reuse and checks launch failure status/exit/context.
TestProcessSessionPathOverride verifies program lookup honors the supplied environment PATH.
TestShellClassPathPrefersCurrentAndExplicitClasses checks modern default Shell and user override precedence, with fallback paths propagated to children.
TestProcessRejectsMalformedStarts verifies malformed argument vectors, nonstring command/directory and missing arguments signal before execution.
TestProcessOutputExactLimitReportsTruncation checks combined and separate stream markers at the exact cap boundary.
TestShellHomeUsesSessionEnvironment checks distinct session home overrides, home expansion and explicit error when home is unset.
